---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const title = "CV";
const description =
  "CV for John Kilpatrick — Optical Engineer @ Oxford Instruments Andor, PhD Physics.";
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="print-bar">
    <p>Prefer a PDF? Use your browser's print dialog and save as PDF.</p>
    <button class="print-button" id="print-btn" type="button">
      Print / Save as PDF
    </button>
  </div>

  <article class="cv-page">
    <header class="cv-header">
      <h1>John Kilpatrick</h1>
      <p class="cv-tagline">Optical Engineer &middot; PhD Physics</p>
      <p class="cv-links">
        Belfast &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
        <a href="/contact">Contact me</a>
        &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
        <a rel="external" href="//linkedin.com/in/rjkilpatrick">LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="cv-summary">
      <p>
        Optical Engineer at Oxford Instruments Andor with over a year of
        experience, seeking new opportunities beginning July 2025. Contributing
        to the development of accurate automated testing for cameras.
        Collaborated with cross-functional teams to optimize hardware control,
        data analysis, and continuous testing platforms, ensuring rapid and
        reliable tests. With a PhD in Physics and a strong background in
        fundamental optics, data processing, and experimental design, driven to
        bridge research and applied engineering. Passionate about delivering
        innovative solutions that enhance quality control processes and advance
        cutting-edge optical technologies. Available to work anywhere in the UK
        or EU.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <h3>Optical Engineer &middot; Oxford Instruments Andor</h3>
          <span class="cv-dates">May 2024 &ndash; Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Provided continuous support to live products through the factory for
            the iStar, iXon, and iVac camera platforms.
          </li>
          <li>
            Supported continuous performance improvements for incremental
            product improvements.
          </li>
          <li>
            Collaborated within a cross-functional team to maintain a robust
            quality test suite for existing products, focusing on scalable,
            production-ready solutions for performance validation.
          </li>
          <li>
            Refined optical test procedures and automated performance validation
            used in manufacturing, ensuring high product quality and consistency
            across volume production through the factory.
          </li>
          <li>
            Performed in-depth optical characterization and diagnostics to
            resolve complex system-level issues, enhancing the reliability and
            imaging capabilities of high-sensitivity detectors.
          </li>
          <li>
            Contribute to enhancement roadmaps for core product lines, aligning
            test development with evolving customer and scientific requirements
            in spectroscopy, microscopy, and time-resolved applications.
          </li>
          <li>
            Promptly responding to customer queries with deep technical insight.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Education</h2>

      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <h3>PhD Physics &middot; University of Exeter</h3>
          <span class="cv-dates">Sept. 2020 &ndash; May 2024</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Research focused on imaging through multimode optical fibres for
          next-generation flexible micro-endoscopes. Developed numerical
          simulations to enhance control over light propagation in multimode
          fibres and experimentally verified results. Presented a talk at
          Frontiers in Optics 2022 and posters at several international
          conferences.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Used Python, MATLAB, and LabVIEW for detailed analysis and
            modelling, aligning experimental results with theoretical
            predictions.
          </li>
          <li>
            Worked independently to troubleshoot complex experimental and
            computational challenges.
          </li>
          <li>
            Strong technical writing and critical thinking applied across a
            range of research scenarios.
          </li>
          <li>
            Managed research objectives, set timelines, and oversaw budget
            planning.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h4>Teaching &amp; Outreach</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Teaching Assistant (2021&ndash;2023):</strong> Supported undergraduate
            teaching in scientific programming (Python). Explained complex ideas clearly,
            marked assignments, and provided constructive feedback.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong
              >President, Exeter Photonics Society (2022&ndash;2023):</strong
            >
            Revamped branding, organized and chaired online talks with international
            speakers, and led a company visit to Effect Photonics. Presented research
            at the Torbay Hi-Tech Cluster. Organized and ran public outreach events:
            stalls at the IOP Festival of Physics (2021) and Pint of Science (2022);
            chaired talks at Pint of Science 2023. Organized a stargazing trip to
            Dartmoor for over 60 people.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <h3>
            MPhys Physics, with study in New Zealand &middot; University of
            Exeter
          </h3>
          <span class="cv-dates">2016 &ndash; 2020</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          First-class honours. Research project aimed to use Raman spectroscopy
          to detect breast cancer in situ. Relevant modules include Scientific
          Programming in C (95%), Computer Graphics (91%), and Advanced Web
          Development (90%).
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
      <ul class="cv-skills">
        <li>Python programming</li>
        <li>Statistical analysis</li>
        <li>Data analysis &amp; visualisation</li>
        <li>Optical experiment design</li>
        <li>Presentation skills</li>
        <li>Science communication</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  document
    .getElementById("print-btn")
    ?.addEventListener("click", () => window.print());
</script>

<style lang="scss">
  .print-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;

    p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
  }

  .print-button {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background-color: var(--accent-1);
    color: white;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;

    &:hover {
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
  }

  .cv-page {
    max-width: 210mm;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    padding: 16mm;
    background-color: white;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 15%);

    a {
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }
  }

  .cv-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;

    h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 2.25rem;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }
  }

  .cv-tagline {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #444;
  }

  .cv-links {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #444;
  }

  .cv-summary {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;

    p {
      margin: 0;
    }
  }

  section + section {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #ddd;
    padding-bottom: 0.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    break-after: avoid;
  }

  h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.35rem;
    break-after: avoid;
  }

  .cv-entry {
    + .cv-entry {
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  .cv-entry__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    break-after: avoid;
    break-inside: avoid;

    h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }
  }

  .cv-dates {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #555;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;

    li {
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      break-inside: avoid;
    }
  }

  .cv-skills {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;

    li {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background-color: #f0f0f0;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
  }

  @media print {
    .print-bar {
      display: none;
    }

    .cv-page {
      max-width: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-shadow: none;
      border-radius: 0;
    }
  }

  @page {
    size: a4;
    margin: 16mm;
  }
</style>
